---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { featuredProjects } from '../data/projects';
import { links } from '../data/links';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="bsquidwrd"
  description="Squid. I write software for a living and build Discord bots and Twitch tooling on my own time."
>
  <section class="intro">
    <img src="/avatar.jpg" alt="" width="92" height="92" />
    <div class="intro-body">
      <p class="eyebrow">bsquidwrd</p>
      <h1>Hey, I&rsquo;m Squid.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I write software for a living. Some of it is our product, some of it is the tool we use to
        get customers set up, and a lot of it is the AWS and Terraform underneath. On my own time I
        build Discord bots and Twitch tooling.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>
      Most of what I publish grows out of a problem I hit myself. <a
        href="https://github.com/bsquidwrd/LiveBot">LiveBot</a
      > started because I wanted my Discord server to know when I went live without me having to say
      so, and it has been the project I keep coming back to. The rest is a mix of Twitch API
      experiments, small utilities for other admins, and whatever I am learning at the time.
    </p>
    <p>
      The day job splits three ways. Some of it is feature work in our flagship product. Some is an
      internal management tool the team uses to configure how each customer&rsquo;s setup runs. The
      rest is the layer underneath all of it: Terraform, AWS, and the pipelines that get everything
      deployed. Moving between the three is the part I like, because a problem looks different from
      inside the application than it does from the infrastructure holding the application up.
    </p>
    <p>
      Away from work it is Go, C#, Python, and a homelab that mostly exists so I have somewhere to
      break things safely.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Selected projects</h2>
    <ul class="card-list">
      {
        featuredProjects.map((project) => (
          <li>
            <a class="card" href={project.url}>
              <div class="card-head">
                <h3>{project.name}</h3>
                <span class="meta">
                  {project.language && <span class="tag">{project.language}</span>}
                  {project.stars ? <span>{project.stars} &#9733;</span> : null}
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>{project.description}</p>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="more"><a href="/projects">See everything &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <ul class="links">
      {
        links.map((link) => (
          <li>
            <a class="link-row" href={link.href}>
              <Icon name={link.icon} />
              <span>
                {link.label}
                <small>{link.note}</small>
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
